      "text": "William Masters didn't just build a plantation in 1863; he established a lasting social structure. Dividing the land and responsibilities among the three family branches is likely what kept this settlement from collapsing over the last century.",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-15T01:28:59Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
